        "summary":  "The article argues that AI agents must move beyond simple communication to achieve genuine coordination and shared understanding. While connecting autonomous agents across organizational boundaries represents meaningful progress, the real challenge lies in enabling them to align on goals, resolve conflicts, and reason together — a problem Cisco\u0027s Outshift calls the \u0027Internet of Cognition.\u0027",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise multi-agent deployments are hitting a ceiling: connecting agents via APIs is solvable, but enabling them to reason jointly, resolve conflicting objectives, and maintain coherent shared state is an unsolved problem at scale. Cisco\u0027s Outshift framing of an \u0027Internet of Cognition\u0027 is a useful mental model for the next orchestration challenge — shifting from message-passing architectures to genuine cognitive collaboration between agents. For enterprise AI leaders planning multi-agent workflows across business units or partner ecosystems, this article is a timely warning that current integration patterns will not scale to complex, cross-boundary reasoning tasks. Evaluate orchestration vendors on their roadmap for shared reasoning, not just connectivity.",
